ly increasing toxicity risk. This highlights the importance of patient counseling regarding dietary intake during macrolide therapy. [Data: Relationships (50532)]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"克林霉素 presents distinct safety profile despite structural similarities\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Although 克林霉素 is sometimes grouped with macrolides in clinical discussions, it belongs to the lincosamide class and exhibits a different interaction profile. It is notably associated with 伪膜性肠炎, a severe form of antibiotic-associated colitis, especially if antidiarrheal agents like diphenoxylate are used concurrently. Furthermore, it demonstrates antagonism when combined with macrolides, reducing mutual efficacy. This distinction is critical for appropriate antimicrobial selection. [Data: Entities (3772); Relationships (9109, 10891)]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Interactions with statins pose muscle toxicity risks\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Co-administration of 大环内酯类药 with 他汀类药 (statins) increases the risk of myopathy, as noted in drug labeling for rosuvastatin. While some macrolides like erythromycin may reduce rosuvastatin exposure, the overall class is flagged for potential enhancement of statin-related muscle toxicity. This interaction necessitates caution when prescribing macrolides to patients on lipid-lowering therapy. [Data: Relationships (28486)]\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"rating\": 7.2,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The community poses a moderate-to-high impact due to widespread, clinically significant drug interactions and hepatotoxicity risks associated with commonly prescribed macrolide antibiotics.\"\n}", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null, "provider_specific_fields": {"refusal": null}}, "provider_specific_fields": {}}], "created": 1782127757, "model": "qwen3-max", "object": "chat.completion", "moderation": null, "service_ti